---
import FormFeed from '../components/FormFeed.astro';
import MemoHeader from '../components/MemoHeader.astro';
import Sec from '../components/Sec.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR, SOCIALS, getWork, memoNumber } from '../lib/memo';

const work = await getWork();
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
const DOC = 'RFC 0';
const SHORT = 'Portfolio';
const DECRYPT = new Set(['firefly', 'noon']);

const stack = String.raw`
+--------+       +----------+       +---------+       +--------+
|  idea  |------>| protocol |------>| product |------>| people |
+--------+       +----------+       +---------+       +--------+
`.slice(1);

const toc = [
	{ id: 'introduction', num: '1', title: 'Introduction', pg: 2 },
	{ id: 'conventions', num: '2', title: 'Conventions Used in This Document', pg: 2 },
	{
		id: 'work',
		num: '3',
		title: 'Work',
		pg: 3,
		children: work.map((p, i) => ({ id: p.id, num: `3.${i + 1}`, title: p.data.title, pg: 3 })),
	},
	{ id: 'security', num: '4', title: 'Security Considerations', pg: 4 },
	{ id: 'iana', num: '5', title: 'IANA Considerations', pg: 4 },
	{ id: 'references', num: '6', title: 'References', pg: 4 },
	{ id: 'address', title: "Author's Address", pg: 4 },
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Sri Pranav Tene — RFC 0: Private Products and Fast Systems"
	description="Sri Pranav Tene is a software engineer and the founder of Lupyd, building privacy-first products, end-to-end encrypted messaging, and peer-to-peer systems."
>
	<MemoHeader
		left={['Independent Submission', 'Request for Comments: 0', 'Obsoletes: v1', 'Category: Informational']}
		title="Sri Pranav Tene: Private Products and Fast Systems"
		docname="draft-tene-portfolio-latest"
	/>

	<Sec id="abstract" title="Abstract">
		<p>
			This memo documents the work of Sri Pranav Tene, a software engineer based in Hyderabad and the
			founder of Lupyd. It covers a privacy-first social platform, end-to-end encrypted messaging,
			peer-to-peer transport, and a handful of smaller tools, and describes how to start a
			collaboration with the author.
		</p>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="status" title="Status of This Memo">
		<p>
			This document is not an Internet Standards Track specification. It is published for
			informational purposes, <mark class="circle">and for hiring.</mark>
		</p>
		<p>
			This is a living document and may be updated, replaced, or obsoleted at any time. Comments are
			welcome at <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>. Distribution of this memo is
			unlimited.
		</p>
		<aside class="note" style="--tilt:-4deg">hiring? my address is at the very bottom</aside>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="copyright" title="Copyright Notice">
		<p>
			Copyright (c) {year} {AUTHOR.name}. The source of this page is available under the MIT License
			at <a href="https://github.com/ash-hashtag/portfolio">github.com/ash-hashtag/portfolio</a>.
		</p>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="toc" title="Table of Contents">
		<ol class="toc">
			{
				toc.map((s) => (
					<li>
						<span class="row">
							<a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.num ? `${s.num}.  ${s.title}` : s.title}</a>
							<span class="pg">{s.pg}</span>
						</span>
						{s.children && (
							<ol>
								{s.children.map((c) => (
									<li>
										<span class="row">
											<a href={`#${c.id}`}>{`${c.num}.  ${c.title}`}</a>
											<span class="pg">{c.pg}</span>
										</span>
									</li>
								))}
							</ol>
						)}
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ol>
	</Sec>

	<FormFeed doc={DOC} short={SHORT} />

	<Sec id="introduction" num="1" title="Introduction">
		<p>
			The author works in the layer where hard technical ideas become dependable products: the part
			after the whiteboard and before the user notices anything at all.
		</p>
		<figure>
			<pre>{stack}</pre>
			<figcaption>Figure 1: Where the author works</figcaption>
		</figure>
		<aside class="note" style="--tilt:-3deg">the middle two are the fun part</aside>
		<p>
			Most of that work happens at Lupyd [<a href="#ref-lupyd">LUPYD</a>], a privacy-focused social and
			collaboration platform built from the ground up: Rust on the server, React and Tauri on the
			clients, and MLS, WebSockets, WebTransport and WebRTC in between. Outside it, the author writes
			Rust, C++, TypeScript, Flutter and Go, and has shipped audio processing, GPU compute, mobile
			apps, smart contracts and a programming language.
		</p>
		<p>
			Section 3 lists the work. A longer account of the author is filed separately as
			<a href="/about/">RFC 1</a>.
		</p>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="conventions" num="2" title="Conventions Used in This Document">
		<p>
			The key words "<span class="kw">MUST</span>", "<span class="kw">MUST NOT</span>", "<span class="kw">SHOULD</span>", "<span class="kw">SHOULD NOT</span>", and "<span class="kw">MAY</span>" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14
			[<a href="#ref-rfc2119">RFC2119</a>] [<a href="#ref-rfc8174">RFC8174</a>] when, and only when,
			they appear in all capitals, as shown here.
		</p>
		<p>The author's own work is held to the following:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>User data <span class="kw">MUST NOT</span> be collected merely because it can be.</li>
			<li>Encryption <span class="kw">SHOULD</span> be <mark class="circle">end-to-end</mark>. The server is not a trusted party.</li>
			<li>A round trip that can be removed <span class="kw">SHOULD</span> be removed.</li>
			<li>A dependency <span class="kw">MAY</span> be added when it pays rent.</li>
			<li>
				Code <span class="kw">MUST</span> remain understandable by whoever maintains it next, including
				the author in a year.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<aside class="note" style="--tilt:2deg">read these as promises, not slogans</aside>
	</Sec>

	<FormFeed doc={DOC} short={SHORT} />

	<Sec id="work" num="3" title="Work">
		<p>
			Projects are listed in order of priority. Each has a full memo with a figure and references;
			the complete list is in the <a href="/work/">index</a>.
		</p>
		{
			work.map((p, i) => (
				<Sec sub id={p.id} num={`3.${i + 1}`} title={p.data.title}>
					<p data-decrypt={DECRYPT.has(p.id) ? '' : undefined}>{p.data.description}</p>
					<p class="meta-line">
						Keywords: {p.data.tags.filter((t) => t !== 'Dev').join(', ')}
						<br />
						Full memo: <a href={`/work/${p.id}/`}>RFC {memoNumber(i)}</a>
						{p.data.githubUrl && (
							<>
								{' · '}Source: <a href={p.data.githubUrl}>{p.data.githubUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>
							</>
						)}
						{p.data.url && (
							<>
								{' · '}Live: <a href={p.data.url}>{p.data.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>
							</>
						)}
					</p>
				</Sec>
			))
		}
	</Sec>

	<FormFeed doc={DOC} short={SHORT} />

	<Sec id="security" num="4" title="Security Considerations">
		<p>
			Projects handed to the author will be asked for a threat model before they are asked for a
			deadline.
		</p>
		<aside class="note" style="--tilt:-2deg">I mean it.</aside>
		<p>
			Mail sent to the address in this memo is not end-to-end encrypted. For anything sensitive, ask
			for a secure channel first.
		</p>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="iana" num="5" title="IANA Considerations">
		<p>This document has no IANA actions. It does request a conversation; see Author's Address.</p>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="references" num="6" title="References">
		<Sec sub id="normative" num="6.1" title="Normative References">
			<dl class="defs">
				<dt id="ref-rfc2119">[RFC2119]</dt>
				<dd>
					Bradner, S., "Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels", BCP 14, RFC 2119,
					March 1997, <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119">&lt;https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119&gt;</a>.
				</dd>
				<dt id="ref-rfc8174">[RFC8174]</dt>
				<dd>
					Leiba, B., "Ambiguity of Uppercase vs Lowercase in RFC 2119 Key Words", BCP 14, RFC 8174,
					May 2017, <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8174">&lt;https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8174&gt;</a>.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</Sec>
		<Sec sub id="informative" num="6.2" title="Informative References">
			<dl class="defs">
				<dt id="ref-lupyd">[LUPYD]</dt>
				<dd><a href="https://www.lupyd.com">&lt;https://www.lupyd.com&gt;</a></dd>
				{
					SOCIALS.map((s) => (
						<>
							<dt>[{s.label.toUpperCase()}]</dt>
							<dd><a href={s.href}>&lt;{s.href}&gt;</a></dd>
						</>
					))
				}
			</dl>
		</Sec>
	</Sec>

	<Sec id="address" title="Author's Address">
		<p>
			{AUTHOR.name}<br />
			{AUTHOR.org}<br />
			{AUTHOR.city}<br />
			<br />
			Email: <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a><br />
			URI: &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/">https://{AUTHOR.site}/</a>
		</p>
	</Sec>

	<FormFeed doc={DOC} short={SHORT} last />
</BaseLayout>
